<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">01 · PERFORMER PHILOSOPHY</p><h2>This is a rehearsal room.</h2>
<p>This isn't a comedy club. You come to work. Get on stage. Leave it there. Improve. Go home.</p>
<p>Everybody starts somewhere. Start here. First attempt or touring set, every minute exists to help you become a better performer. Help reset the room or cheer for another comic if you want; getting your reps and leaving is welcome too.</p>
<p>Your original material stays yours. The room should leave you stronger than when you arrived.</p></article>

<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">02 · ARRIVAL + PARKING</p><h2>Arrive 10–20 minutes before.</h2>
<p>Do not arrive more than 20 minutes before your stage time. Check in immediately upon arrival and be on deck by ten minutes before your set. Arriving at T−10 means checking in and being ready at once.</p>
<p>BOX2 spaces are for actively arriving or departing performers. Use only host-designated BOX2 bays. If full, contact the host; do not improvise parking in residential, shared, or access areas. Keep driveways clear. Notify the host about a blocking vehicle instead of confronting its driver.</p>
<p><?= e(config()['venue_public_enabled'] ? config()['arrival_text'] : 'Parking permissions, routes, and exact bays are awaiting onsite verification. No parking map or walk-in access is approved for publication.') ?></p></article>

<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">03 · FINDING BOX2</p><h2>Follow verified arrival instructions.</h2>
<p>Use the host-reviewed parking, walking, and entry walkthrough once it is published. Do not assume a map pin identifies the performance entrance or that a neighboring lot provides access.</p>
<p><?= config()['venue_public_enabled'] ? 'Check your booking receipt and arrival page for the approved instructions and text walkthrough.' : 'Entry routes and accessible entrance details are not yet published. Await verified host instructions; this preview is not an invitation to walk in.' ?></p></article>

<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">04 · CHECK-IN FLOW</p><h2>Check in as you arrive.</h2>
<p>Your arrival window is T−20 through T−10. Check in upon arrival. Be on deck in the lobby/front desk area at T−10, ready to perform. This is not a guaranteed late-arrival grace period.</p>
<p>Wait in the lobby until called. Only the performer currently on deck enters the immediate staging area; the next performer rotates in as the previous performer rotates out. Keep movement clear and considerate.</p></article>

<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">05 · PERFORMANCE ENVIRONMENT</p><h2>Bring focus back to the joke.</h2>
<p>This is a workspace being improved. Equipment, maintenance activity, dogs, and outside or rail noise may be present. Distractions are a chance to practice recovering your focus.</p>
<p>Noise is not permission for unsafe conditions. Tell the host about hazards; staff must address them or stop access. Acknowledging this card does not make construction hazards acceptable.</p></article>

<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">06 · HEALTH + FACILITY</p><h2>Cleaning is an operating duty.</h2>
<p>Hosts log compatible microphone and shared-surface cleaning between performers, plus hourly lobby and stage-left bathroom high-touch cleaning. Follow product instructions and actual contact times; provide hand hygiene.</p>
<p>If you feel ill, stay home and cancel or reschedule. Cleaning records do not certify a sterile or infection-free space. Public bookings stay closed until premises and access are verified.</p></article>

<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">07 · SOBER ROOM CULTURE</p><h2>Respect the work.</h2>
<p>No alcohol or drugs. Original comedy only: stand-up, sketches/characters, host practice, and musical comedy with an instrument you can carry in and out yourself.</p>
<p>Respect the clock, the next performer, volunteers, and neighbors. No attacking a prior comic to steal laughs, talking in back, disruptive phone use, or unauthorized filming. This room belongs to the act on stage.</p></article>

<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">08 · AUDIENCE + RECORDING</p><h2>Your set. Your choices.</h2>
<p>Spectating is welcome and optional. There is no obligation to linger or socialize; leaving promptly makes room for the next performer. Focus on stage time. Socialize online.</p>
<p>Choose livestream, archive, approved host clips, adaptation, and moderated feedback separately; all begin off. Approved candidates may be considered for clips, never automatically or with a guarantee.</p>
<p>BOX2 archive retention is <?= (int)config()['vod_retention_days'] ?> days under the stated policy. Live-only means the host disables Twitch VOD and local recording. Private rehearsal requires streaming and all recording actually stopped. The website cannot control OBS or cameras; independent viewer copies may persist.</p></article>

<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">09 · THE BOX2 MINDSET</p><h2>Leave your best set on stage.</h2>
<p>BOX2 is where rough material gets sharpened. A dog may bark, a train may pass, or someone may cough. Return attention to the joke. Leave your ego at the door, then go build the next one.</p>
<p>You keep ownership of your material. A recorded set can document when it was performed; it cannot prove global first authorship, copyright registration, or theft. Come Tell It Here First.</p></article>
